LISA barrier_of_system_scope_orders_nothing
(* A barrier has subgroup, block or device scope. A barrier of system scope does not make the
   threads wait for each other, so the read races with the write.
   Expect: sometimes, a data race. *)
{ x = 0; }
 P0                | P1                ;
 w[plain] x 1      | f[barrier,system] ;
 f[barrier,system] | r[plain] r0 x     ;
scopes: (device (block P0 P1))
exists (1:r0 = 0)
